// HAS_PART, CONTAINS_SET, HAS_INVENTORY, CONTAINS_MINIFIG.

// Actually, it's easier to think of the "content" nodes as Set, Minifig, Part.
// The root is a Set.
// Path: (Set)-[:HAS_INVENTORY]->(Inv)
// From Inv, we can go to Part (end), Set (continue), Minifig (continue).
// If we go to Set: (Set)-[:HAS_INVENTORY]->(Inv) ...
// If we go to Minifig: (Minifig)-[:HAS_INVENTORY]->(Inv) ...

